# Next.js static-export output.
#
# This line was previously written in UTF-16LE, with a null byte between every
# character, so git read it as fourteen meaningless bytes and it matched nothing.
# It was also redundant: frontend/.gitignore has carried /out/ since the Next.js
# scaffold, and that is the rule which actually fires. Kept here anyway, now in
# plain UTF-8, so the intent is readable from the root of the repository.
#
# NOTE: frontend/out/ is nonetheless TRACKED - 33 files, committed deliberately
# in 7d72641 for the old static-export rsync deploy, which deploy.yml no longer
# uses. An ignore rule has no effect on paths already in the index, so those
# files stay until someone removes them. That is a separate decision.
frontend/out/

# Audit harness: test scripts, screenshots and a database dump with real user
# data. Useful locally, must never reach the repository or the production server.
audit/

# Other clients' deliverables - work that happens to be written inside this
# folder but does not belong to this project. Previously this showed up as
# untracked clutter in every `git status`.
#
# The contents are excluded rather than the folder itself, because git cannot
# re-include anything inside an excluded DIRECTORY - the negations below would
# silently do nothing if this said `deliverables/`.
deliverables/*

# ...except the USDA database dump, which IS this project's. It is the only
# way to load the food tables onto a host with no shell, it is 392 KB, and the
# data is public domain (CC0), so it belongs in the repository rather than
# being emailed around. Tracked deliberately, not by accident.
!deliverables/usda/
deliverables/usda/*
!deliverables/usda/usda_local_foods.sql.gz
